{
  "id": "jungle-white-border-test-print",
  "name": "Jungle white border test print",
  "category": "test",
  "description": {
    "text": "Jungle's 16 non-holo rares with a white border instead of a yellow one. The yellow border is printed as a separate solid layer, and on these it was left off; the rest is the finished unlimited Jungle card. They come from uncut sheets of the non-holo rares, one of them marked in the margin \"Yaquinto Job #1773, 8-9-99, Wizards – Jungle 4, Form 4, Rare\": August 1999, about two months after Jungle came out. Whether the run was a deliberate test or a sheet missing an ink layer isn't known.\n\nThe man who cut them up said he had bought two such sheets years earlier, one already torn in half, and cut up the intact one himself, which is why the borders are uneven. 50 of the cards were auctioned through Probstein123 in May 2024, graded by CGC as test prints; PSA authenticates them too, with \"hand cut\" on the label.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Probstein123 auctions 50 white border Jungle test prints",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/probstein123-auctions-50-white-border-jungle-test-prints/48095"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: white border Jungle thread, the cutter's account",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/probstein123-auctions-50-white-border-jungle-test-prints/48095/73"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Test Print cards from Jungle (dated sheet)",
